pseudo-Boolean proof version 2.0
* Regression test (wrong verdict): the differential partner of
* correct/version2/redundance_empty_witness_proofgoal_contradiction. Same
* formula, same `red` with an empty witness, but the subproof discharges a
* DATABASE proofgoal instead of goal `#1`.
*
* Discharging database goal 1 shows `DB /\ ~C /\ ~C_1 |- false`, and since
* `C_1` is in `DB` its negation is refuted for free -- it says nothing about
* `DB /\ ~C`. `end_proofgoal` used to set `contradiction_proven` for ANY
* discharged goal inside a proof-by-contradiction subproof, so this bought the
* whole subproof and `red` added the empty contradiction `>= 1`. The formula
* here happens to be unsatisfiable, so the verdict is not itself wrong -- what
* is wrong is that the step is licensed at all, and
* incorrect/version2/redundance_empty_witness_proofgoal_not_contradiction shows
* the same move refuting a SATISFIABLE formula.
f 4
red >= 1 ; ; begin
	proofgoal 1
		p -1 1 +
	end -1
end
u >= 1 ;
output NONE
conclusion UNSAT : -1
end pseudo-Boolean proof
